@model string
@* A recovery key just made, shown the one time it can be (Pages/RecoveryKey, and Pages/ChangePassword after a first
   password). The download posts the key back to /RecoveryKey, which checks it before building the recovery file. *@
<section class="panel recovery-panel">
    <h2>Your recovery key</h2>
    <p><code class="setup-key recovery-key">@Model</code></p>
    <p>If you ever forget your password, this key lets you set a new one yourself from <em>Forgotten your password?</em> on the sign-in page. Save it now - <strong>this is the only time it is shown</strong>. Download the recovery file and keep it somewhere only you can get to, such as a password manager or a private folder, or print this page and lock it away. Not on a shared drive, and not in an email.</p>
    <div class="button-row heading-actions">
        <form method="post" asp-page="/RecoveryKey" asp-page-handler="Download"><input type="hidden" name="key" value="@Model" /><button class="button button-primary">Download recovery file</button></form>
        <button class="button button-secondary" type="button" data-action="print">Print it</button>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="/">I've saved it</a>
    </div>
</section>
